** After a two-over-one response

A two-over-one response promises another bid, so opener's rebid only has to
describe the hand: a new suit (a reverse included) is 4+ cards and forcing, a
raise of responder's suit is 4+ cards (3+ for a 2!h response, which shows five),
2NT is a minimum balanced hand and 3NT a balanced 18--19, a jump rebid of the
opening suit shows six cards and extra values, and a plain rebid of the opening
suit is the minimum with nothing else to show (NOTES.md #C1).

