** After a raise or a notrump response

After a single raise of a major, opener passes a minimum, invites with a
medium hand and bids game with a maximum; after a limit raise, opener passes a
bare minimum and otherwise bids game. After the Jacoby 2NT raise, opener shows a
singleton or void at the three level, a good second five-card suit at the four
level, and otherwise describes strength: 3 of the major is 18+, 3NT is 15--17 and
4 of the major is a minimum. After a non-forcing 1NT response, opener passes a
balanced minimum and otherwise rebids naturally, a reverse or a jump shift
showing extra values.

